B.cx4=new A.d1("sidescroller","A real-time side-scrolling platformer with its own game loop (joystick + jump/attack); optional high-score persistence.",B.bie,!1)
B.cWF=new A.p("cols",B.af,"Grid columns (default 36).",B.f,null)
B.cWo=new A.p("rows",B.af,"Grid rows (default 24).",B.f,null)
B.cIW=new A.p("seed",B.af,"World seed \u2014 same seed reproduces the same terrain (share to compare designs).",B.f,null)
B.bCG=s([B.cWF,B.cWo,B.cIW],t.G)
B.cw0=new A.d1("noms","Opens on a TITLE MENU (New game/Custom/Single player/Multiplayer/Settings/Info) over the gameplay dimmed. A controllable real-time RTS: pan/zoom a world, TAP-select or BOX-select noms and command them (move/attack). DESIGN THE FLOW by painting ZONES (Gather/Grow/Guard/Home) with a per-zone flow target \u2014 noms self-organise to fill them and ferry food into a shared GRANARY. MOVE the tribe with \ud83d\udccd Rally flags (one tap each, no selecting; drop several and each nom heads to the nearest). GAME MODES: open-ended Sandbox (harmony/domination are celebrations, not game-enders) or a timed Speed Run. BUILD A CITY: place blueprints of fictional-tech buildings (burrow/glow-post/larder/moot-hall) and the noms construct them from granary food \u2014 finished buildings cheer + speed the town. Set POLICIES (share food, cooperate, build tunnels, self-control, or delegate to the noms) \u2014 and balance the society: both scarcity AND abundance breed greed, violence and DEVOLUTION, so aim for the middle. A coach hint, pause/speed and a balance meter keep it legible. Dig water to grow trees; miracles noms LEARN; two tribes fight. A CULTURE SIM: each nom carries a cultural identity + values that spread to neighbours, inherit across generations and DIVERGE into distinct cultures (toggle the culture view to see them). Cultures CLASH or BLEND at their borders and grow traits \u2014 a Rite of Sharing or a Taboo of Hoarding \u2014 that shape how they share and cooperate (the culture view shows the seams). AUTOPLAY: an auto-keeper (\ud83e\udd16) grows a thriving, balanced colony itself \u2014 digs water, populates, lays zones, tunes policies and builds. A \ud83d\udcac LIVE NARRATION feed explains what is happening and WHY (every autoplay decision states its reason), an adjustable SPEED control fast-forwards 1\xd7\u21928\xd7 (sub-stepped so it stays stable), and a one-tap FULL AUTO-RUN starts a self-running, narrated, fast-forwarded society to just sit back and watch. Seed-based reproducible worlds. Touch + mouse + web.",B.bCG,!1)
B.cUE=new A.p("seed",B.af,"World seed - same seed reproduces the same resource field.",B.f,null)
B.cTj=new A.p("saveTable",B.at,'Table holding campaign save rows (default "campaign").',B.f,null)
B.bjE=s([B.cUE,B.cTj],t.G)
B.cww=new A.d1("spacegame","TETHERFIELD - a real-time build-a-power-grid, mine, and defend game (an original homage to the classic The Space Game). Drop MODULES into a resource field; they AUTO-LINK to neighbours within range to form a power web. GENERATORS make energy, RELAYS carry power + minerals across the web, CELLS bank it, EXTRACTORS on deposits turn power into minerals, and TURRETS (Laser / Pulser / Beam / Lance - each with its own range, the Lance with a MIN range so it cannot hit point-blank) auto-target and defend the CORE against escalating waves of enemies (Darts, Breakers, beam-resistant Toruses, and a Colossus boss). Links GLOW when power flows. Modes: Campaign (a mission chain with objective panel + progress bar, Next-level / Replay / Retry flow, and in-session completion ticks on the mission list), Survival (endless), and Sandbox (free build). Tap to place, Sell to remove for a partial refund. In-memory sandbox.",B.bjE,!1)
B.cX8=new A.p("seed",B.af,"Simulation seed - same seed reproduces the same wave pattern.",B.f,null)
B.bhe=s([B.cX8],t.G)
B.cwX=new A.d1("hesset","HESSET - a GEOMETRY strategy/defense game where the player DRAWS the geometry (deliberately unlike spacegame: no auto-linking). Place shape-NODES - triangle Spikes (shoot at foes), square Anchors (cheap, tough, structural), pentagon Wells (generate FLUX, the single resource), hexagon Prisms (amplifiers) - and DRAG an edge from one shape to another (cost grows with length, capped). CLOSING a loop of edges claims the enclosed polygon as a live FIELD whose role comes from the majority shape in its ring: Spike loops KILL foes inside, Well loops earn flux by AREA, Anchor loops are BASTIONS (the ring resists damage), Prism loops are RESONANT (boost adjacent fields). Hostile shapes attack from the rim - Shards saw through edges, Orbs ram nodes, the slow Mass grinds toward the CORE you must protect. Objectives include the signature CLAIM goal (total enclosed area) and survive-N-waves. Modes: Campaign (teaches one shape at a time), Endless, and Sandbox. Tap to place, drag to draw, Sell to remove for a partial refund. Minimal luminous look. In-memory sandbox.",B.bhe,!1)
B.cKw=new A.p("cols",B.af,"Hex columns (default 22).",B.f,null)
B.cRW=new A.p("rows",B.af,"Hex rows (default 18).",B.f,null)
B.cJi=new A.p("seed",B.af,"World seed (reproducible terrain).",B.f,null)
B.cHU=new A.p("mode",B.E,'Set "siege" for the siege scenario; any other value (or unset) is the default board.',B.f,null)
B.cOZ=new A.p("saveTable",B.at,'Table holding siege save games (default "siegeSaves").',B.f,null)
B.bwT=s([B.cKw,B.cRW,B.cJi,B.cHU,B.cOZ],t.G)
B.cxa=new A.d1("hexnom","A HEX-GRID city game (sibling of noms). Opens on a title menu over a dimmed scene. Dig water so trees grow and feed your noms, then BUILD A CITY: lay a transport network of tiered roads (path/street/avenue) and RAIL, place houses/markets/parks, and send WAGONS, CARS and TRAINS that ROUTE along the network (pathfinding) with lane CAPACITY & CONGESTION (avenues flow, paths jam); trains ride RAIL only. Noms travel faster on better roads. A WATERSHED ECONOMY rides the network: markets turn food into coin, vehicles physically CARRY it to houses (so wealth only reaches what the roads connect), and a rich house funds new noms \u2014 the city grows where money flows. FINANCE: building costs coin from a city treasury (funded by trade taxes); take a BANK LOAN to build now and repay with INTEREST from future flow. AUTOPLAY: an auto-mayor (\ud83e\udd16) develops the whole city itself \u2014 digs water, builds markets/houses/roads, runs vehicles and even takes loans \u2014 so you can just watch. PASSENGERS ride too: STATIONS (\ud83d\ude89) gather travel demand from nearby noms, and BUSES (\ud83d\ude8c)/cars/trains board them and pay FARES into the city on arrival \u2014 people move value just like freight. BROKERAGE: INVEST treasury capital into a market for ongoing DIVIDENDS that grow it (distinct from a bank loan, which costs interest). MULTI-SCALE VIEW: zoom OUT to a REGION map where each NEIGHBOURHOOD is a node sized by its MONEY with a \u25b2/\u25bc NET growth badge and TRANSIT flows (\ud83d\ude9a) between districts; zoom IN for the detailed hex sim. The auto-mayor narrates itself: a \ud83d\udcac LIVE NARRATION feed explains each decision and WHY, speed is adjustable (1\xd7/2\xd7/4\xd7/8\xd7), and a one-tap FULL AUTO-RUN starts the auto-mayor + narration + a brisk speed together so a whole city builds itself while you watch. Pointy-top odd-r hexes; camera pan/zoom; touch + mouse + web. In-memory sandbox.",B.bwT,!1)
B.cYO=new A.p("table",B.at,"The dataset the default controls target.",B.f,null)
B.bmT=s(["auto","left","right","top","bottom"],t.s)
B.cTC=new A.p("dock",B.bF,"Where the controls dock around the body. auto (default) = side panel on wide surfaces; on phones every dock becomes a floating button PILL (bottom-center, raised clear of the OS gesture zone) that opens the controls as a HALF-height draggable sheet \u2014 the content stays partially visible; drag the sheet's top handle to expand, close via \xd7, downward fling, or barrier tap.",B.bmT,null)
B.cPw=new A.p("sheetLabel",B.E,'Label for the phone pill + the region header (default: the localized engine builtin "Data controls"); may be a {lang: text} map.',B.f,null)
B.cYm=new A.p("body",B.V,"The board content the controls dock around (a node spec). Omit to render just the control strip.",B.f,null)
B.d04=new A.p("children",B.V,"Explicit control-block node specs (default: filter + group + sort for `table`).",B.f,null)
B.cYJ=new A.p("blocksTable",B.at,'Opt-in table of USER-ADDED control-block rows (columns: id, kind [filter|group|sort|range|segment|search], column?, label?, order). When set, the dock gains an "Add control" affordance (+ button) and a per-block remove (\xd7); blocks render from these rows AFTER the static `children`, through the SAME datafilter/datagroup/datasort/datarange/datasegment/datasearch node builders.',B.f,null)
B.bvS=s([B.cYO,B.cTC,B.cPw,B.cYm,B.d04,B.cYJ],t.G)
B.cw9=new A.d1("datacontrols",'The dockable DATA CONTROLS region \u2014 the databoard spine\'s face. Hosts control blocks (children; default = datafilter + datagroup + datasort for `table`) docked around `body`. Controls publish to the board-level shared data config; any view with configSource:"board" subscribes, so filters/grouping/sort persist across chart, table and map representations.',B.bvS,!1)
B.cJf=new A.p("table",B.at,"Dataset the filters apply to.",B.f,null)
B.bwX=s([B.cJf],t.G)
B.cw8=new A.d1("datafilter","CONTROL block: the unified Add-filter bar bound to the BOARD shared data config for `table` \u2014 one filter set that every subscribed view of the dataset obeys.",B.bwX,!1)
B.cJ8=new A.p("table",B.at,"Dataset to group.",B.f,null)
B.bog=s([B.cJ8],t.G)
B.cwS=new A.d1("datagroup","CONTROL block: shared GROUP BY picker (categorical columns only) publishing to the board data config.",B.bog,!1)
B.cUK=new A.p("table",B.at,"Dataset to sort.",B.f,null)
B.bgy=s([B.cUK],t.G)
B.cwP=new A.d1("datasort","CONTROL block: shared SORT picker (column + direction) publishing to the board data config.",B.bgy,!1)
B.cHX=new A.p("table",B.at,"Dataset the range filters.",B.f,null)
B.cZV=new A.p("column",B.t,"Numeric column to bound.",B.f,null)
B.cHs=new A.p("label",B.E,"Label above the slider (default: the column label).",B.f,null)
B.bi1=s([B.cHX,B.cZV,B.cHs],t.G)
B.cwF=new A.d1("datarange","CONTROL block: a numeric RANGE slider over `column` publishing a shared between-filter (full span = no constraint). Drags stay local; release publishes.",B.bi1,!1)
B.d_7=new A.p("min",B.af,"Minimum value (default 0).",B.f,null)
B.cVn=new A.p("max",B.af,"Maximum value (default 100).",B.f,null)
B.cSH=new A.p("step",B.af,"Snap increment. Omitted/0 = continuous (100 divisions).",B.f,null)
B.cVe=new A.p("value",B.af,"Initial value (default: min).",B.f,"Initial value")
B.cMm=new A.p("defaultValue",B.af,"Fallback initial value when value is unset (default: min).",B.f,null)
B.cJx=new A.p("label",B.E,"Label shown above the track; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.f,null)
B.cLK=new A.p("showValue",B.W,"Show the live numeric value beside the label (default true).",B.f,null)
B.cXU=new A.p("setting",B.E,'Board-setting KEY the live value is written to via the same setSetting semantics every control uses (not durable unless allow-listed) \u2014 other nodes read it back live via "$setting:<key>".',B.f,null)
B.cL1=new A.p("action",B.V,'Action spec { fn, args } fired on change; any literal "$value" in args (nested lists/maps included) is substituted with the current number first \u2014 e.g. drives mapSetFilter/mapSetPaint directly with zero extra plumbing.',B.f,null)
B.cS6=new A.p("play",B.W,"Opt-in auto-play/timelapse (default off): shows a play/pause button beside the slider that sweeps the value from the active range's start to its end, advancing by `step` (or 1/100th of the span when step is 0/omitted) every `playIntervalMs`, firing the SAME setting-write / action a manual change fires at every step. Pressing play restarts from the active-range start when the thumb is already at the end, otherwise continues from the current value. Any manual drag pauses playback in place (the `databars` play convention).",B.f,null)
B.anj=new A.p("playIntervalMs",B.af,"Milliseconds between auto-play steps \u2014 default ~1200. Only used with play:true.",B.f,null)
B.cTx=new A.p("playLoop",B.W,"Whether auto-play wraps to the active-range start after reaching the end \u2014 default false (stops and flips the button back to play). Only used with play:true.",B.f,null)
B.bbe=s([B.d_7,B.cVn,B.cSH,B.cVe,B.cMm,B.cJx,B.cLK,B.cXU,B.cL1,B.cS6,B.anj,B.cTx],t.G)
B.cx6=new A.d1("slider",'A minimal, single-value horizontal slider (min/max/step/value from JSON) \u2014 distinct from `datarange` (a dual-thumb column filter): this is a general-purpose control whose live value can write a named board SETTING (`setting`, readable elsewhere via the existing "$setting:<key>" token) and/or fire an arbitrary `action` (any literal "$value" in the action\'s args, however deeply nested, is substituted with the current number before firing) \u2014 e.g. driving `mapSetFilter`/`mapSetPaint` directly to threshold a map choropleth by a live budget value. Either, both, or neither may be set; debounced ~80ms while dragging, always flushed once on release. Opt into `play` for an auto-advance timelapse; a `sliderSetRange` action can constrain the slider to an active sub-range at runtime \u2014 see those props.',B.bbe,!1)
B.cSh=new A.p("hint",B.E,"Placeholder shown when the field is empty; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.f,null)
B.cKA=new A.p("debounceMs",B.af,"Debounce window in ms for the change-fired action (default 350). Submit always fires immediately, uncoupled from this.",B.f,null)
B.d_O=new A.p("action",B.V,'Action spec { fn, args } fired on debounced change and on submit; any literal "$value" in args (nested lists/maps included) is substituted with the field\'s current text first.',B.f,null)
B.cUw=new A.p("focusSignal",B.V,'{table, id, column} \u2014 a value the host BUMPS to command external keyboard focus (e.g. a magnifier "start searching" toggle). Watched every rebuild; any change from the previously seen value requests focus. Optional.',B.f,null)
B.cM2=new A.p("resetSignal",B.V,"{table, id, column} \u2014 same shape as focusSignal, but a change clears the field's own visible text and fires its `action` with an empty string, so bound downstream state clears too. Optional; distinct from focusSignal so one external toggle can choose either behavior per host-side state.",B.f,null)
B.cHe=new A.p("contentPadding",B.V,"{left, top, right, bottom} in px, each optional (default 12 per side \u2014 the ordinary decoration inset). Lets the field's own text inset be pulled in line with unrelated sibling content sharing its row (e.g. list-row titles below it that start flush at the row's own screen inset, with no further indent of their own).",B.f,null)
B.btU=s([B.cSh,B.cKA,B.d_O,B.cUw,B.cM2,B.cHe],t.G)
B.cwy=new A.d1("textinput",'A single-line free-text field \u2014 the `slider` $value-substitution pattern generalized from numeric to text. On every change (debounced) AND on submit (immediate) it can fire an `action` (any literal "$value" in args, however deeply nested, is substituted with the field\'s current text first \u2014 an empty field still fires, so a "clear" is expressible). No table binding of its own; drives whatever action the applet author wires (e.g. a debounced search-as-you-type `http` fetch).',B.btU,!1)
B.cNt=new A.p("table",B.at,"Dataset the chips filter.",B.f,null)
B.cW1=new A.p("column",B.t,"Low-cardinality column.",B.f,null)
B.cJZ=new A.p("label",B.E,"Label above the chips (default: the column label); may be a {lang: text} map.",B.f,null)
B.cPG=new A.p("max",B.af,"Hide when distinct values exceed this (default 8).",B.f,null)
B.cYT=new A.p("valueLabels",B.V,"Opt-in raw-value \u2192 display map for the chip TEXT: {raw: text-or-{lang:text}} (or column-keyed {column: {raw: ...}}), resolved against the ambient locale; unmapped values render raw (passthrough, never blank). The published filter value stays the RAW stored value.",B.f,null)
B.cPy=new A.p("options",B.V,"Fixed List of values to offer INSTEAD of deriving the chip set from the data \u2014 use when the contract fixes the value set (e.g. a range enum) and the data may not yet carry a row for every value (a fresh snapshot with no activity yet for one value must still offer its chip). Skips the derive-from-data pass and the too-few/too-many auto-hide rule. Unset (default) keeps the original derive-from-data behavior, byte-identical.",B.f,null)
B.cTb=new A.p("default",B.E,'Value to select the FIRST time this control is shown for its (table, column) pair \u2014 i.e. while no filter has ever been set. Applied once; a user later toggling every chip off means "no constraint" exactly as before, it never re-snaps to this default. Unset (default) keeps the original empty-selection start, byte-identical.',B.f,null)
B.bou=s([B.cNt,B.cW1,B.cJZ,B.cPG,B.cYT,B.cPy,B.cTb],t.G)
B.cwx=new A.d1("datasegment","CONTROL block: one-tap VALUE CHIPS for a low-cardinality column (scenario/status switch). Multi-select; each tap toggles that value in the shared choice filter; none selected = no constraint. Hides itself when the column is not segment-shaped.",B.bou,!1)
B.cVk=new A.p("table",B.at,"Dataset the bars bucket.",B.f,null)
B.cGO=new A.p("column",B.t,"Column whose distinct values become bars.",B.f,null)
B.cJr=new A.p("colors",B.V,"{ value: rampName } map for per-bar color (same ramp-name vocabulary as the map node's `colors`). Optional \u2014 unmapped values use the theme default.",B.f,null)
B.cN3=new A.p("sectionColumn",B.t,"Optional column whose distinct values group the bars into labeled sections with a separator (e.g. one strip carrying several days' worth of bars).",B.f,null)
B.cNp=new A.p("play",B.W,'Opt-in auto-play cursor (default off): shows a small play/pause button that steps the selection one bar at a time left-to-right across the whole strip (sections group visually but never interrupt the sweep), publishing through the same choice-filter path a manual tap uses so every configSource:"board" subscriber follows the wave. Any manual tap/drag stops play in place.',B.f,null)
B.cQs=new A.p("playLoop",B.W,"Whether auto-play wraps to the first bar after the last \u2014 default true. false stops (and pauses) at the last bar. Only used with play:true.",B.f,null)
B.cIV=new A.p("valueLabels",B.V,"Opt-in raw-value \u2192 display map for bar/section TEXT: {raw: text-or-{lang:text}} or column-keyed {column: {raw: ...}} (sections resolve under `sectionColumn`), locale-aware with raw passthrough. Selection/filter values stay RAW.",B.f,null)
